# Project roast patterns

> Generated/updated by `/roast-learn`. Agents: treat as project law for critiques. Cite evidence when claiming a violation.

**learningMode:** once  
**includeTranscripts:** false  

**Last learned:** 2026-08-06  
**Last transcript scan:** never

## Patterns (prefer)

- Prefer `npx @rapchic/roast install` (no `@latest`) in user-facing docs — `README.md:13`
- Keep `commands/cursor/`, `skills/roast/`, `rules/` as source of truth; sync `.cursor/` via install — `AGENTS.md:28`
- Read package name from `package.json` (`PACKAGE_NAME`) for npm fetch paths — `installer/src/update.js:1`
- Scope roasts to diff budget ≤30 files; ask before expanding — `skills/roast/SKILL.md` hard rule 8

## Antipatterns (avoid)

- Do not put contributor/`npm link` flows in README — `AGENTS.md:14`
- Do not hand-edit generated product copies under `.cursor/commands|skills|rules` (except workspace-only `/roast-no` and `roast-patterns.mdc`) — `AGENTS.md:29`
- Do not invent patterns without `path:line` / convention / transcript evidence — `commands/cursor/roast-learn.md`
- Do not use unscoped `npx roast` — name taken; package is `@rapchic/roast` — `README.md` (Troubleshooting)

## Layout & stack notes

- CLI: `installer/`; skill: `skills/roast/`; Cursor commands: `commands/cursor/`
- Bins after install: `roast` + alias `roastit`
